            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0098" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/314</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-09T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1918, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.49 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2256. The following appears in to-day’s Copenhagen newspapers: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Bolshevik representative of the Russian Government, M.
                                Vorovski, has made the following declaration through the
                            Ritzau [Reuter?] Bureau: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>We hereby give notification to commercial houses and to private
                                    persons who have deposits in Russia that these deposits are
                                    perfectly secure and run no risk whatever of being confiscated
                                    in whole in part. We notify therefore the persons or firms in
                                    question not to withdraw their money by checks at a discount by
                                    which speculators are ready to profit.</p>
                                <p>The Russian Government is now making every effort to [take
                                    measures?] in order that these persons of Russian nationality
                                    now resident in Denmark should receive, through the intermediary
                                    of Danish banks, the sums necessary for their living expenses.
                                    This will be arranged within a short time and the public will be
                                    informed thereof through the press.</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">V.
                                Vorovski</hi></p>
                        <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">May
                                8, 1918.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The foregoing is evidently the outcome of a number of Russian bankers who
                    recently arrived in Copenhagen and a member of the German Reichsbank. Apparently
                    this is another German move towards securing control of Russia, not only of the
                    financial institutions but likewise of commercial houses and particularly of
                    individuals, the majority of whom are nearing the end of their resources and
                    through this maneuver become directly dependent upon the German Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
